===============================================================================
Third-party notice — GNU Unifont glyph bitmaps
===============================================================================

`atc1441_src/Firmware/src/font_unifont.h` is generated by
`tools/gen_v14_tables.py` and contains a 79-glyph *subset* of the GNU Unifont
bitmap font (the Chinese glyphs on rows 1 and 3, plus the ASCII digits and
letters).  The glyphs are converted from the distribution's `.hex` file to
column-major C arrays; no outline data and no hinting is carried over.

GNU Unifont is dual-licensed.  This project uses it under the **SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1** — the full text is vendored at
[`LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt`](LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt), together with the copyright
line and the reserved font name.  The OFL explicitly permits embedding the
font in software and does not extend to the software itself, so the rest of
this repository stays MIT.

The subset is a Modified Version for OFL purposes (glyphs removed, format
changed).  It is therefore not called "Unifont" anywhere in this repository,
and the reserved name is not used to promote it.

Reproduce the exact input used:

    sha256 of the .hex consumed   bebdcabd07a26e1b7162c58c1dc5f43a4c65a303bbcd2a45e3ba41f5ff5f7124
    python tools/gen_v14_tables.py <path to unifont.hex>

Upstream: https://unifoundry.com/unifont/
